    "physics": "none; no fabricated people, coordinate or thermal measurement",
    "max_doors": 5,
    "max_board_records": 10,
    "native_unsafe_door_count": "Native accepts uint8 through255 but owns only five door records; the model rejects effective counts>5 and out-of-range cumulative ACK/final UART indices atomically, including configuration-induced mode changes.",
    "boundary_cache": "Early invalid-border sentinel is [\" \"] (one space); early reset clears cache to empty string. Late always emits an object; both zero-door lists use [\"\"]. Install1 emits left/right/farthest; install2 right/farthest; other install values only list. Config refresh is synchronous synthetic policy.",
    "native_mode_timeouts": "Early modes6 and7 and late mode6 have no queue producer, retain r404. Late mode7 saves/queues successfully without appended coordinates.",
    "module_management": "loginRes requires generic-key selector1; hbok/tm require plaintext selector2, either JSON-string pack or unwrapped. All are silent; loginRes r200 resets heartbeat timer without key replacement. Unwrapped packets retain cached UID/cid. Model validates tm calendar syntax and retains a synthetic module-time input cache; no physical clock/RTOS/cloud-reconnect execution.",
    "ota": "Source selector0 upgrade routes are assessed; model explicitly rejects atomically, never downloads/flashes or reports a fake success.",
